<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<Flow xmlns="http://soap.sforce.com/2006/04/metadata">
    <!--
        THIS COMMENT MUST STAY INSIDE THE ROOT <Flow> ELEMENT - a comment placed ABOVE <Flow>
        breaks `sf` deploy at source conversion.

        SIBLING GUARD ADDED 2026-09-02 (agent-output/three-gaps-design-2026-09-02.md, item 3
        follow-up). Before this change this flow closed the parent Opportunity the moment ANY
        Transaction__c on it reached Status__c = 'Closed', with no regard for siblings. That was
        already a silent bug on any deal with more than one Transaction (closes the deal while
        other work is still open) - item 3's new validation rule
        (Transaction_Closed_Before_Closed_Won, keyed on Has_Open_Transaction__c /
        Has_Closed_Transaction__c) turns that same gap into a hard failure instead: on a
        two-Transaction deal, the FIRST Transaction to close would attempt StageName = 'Closed
        Won' while a sibling is still open, the rule refuses it, and the refusal rolls back the
        TRANSACTION SAVE that triggered this flow (CANNOT_EXECUTE_FLOW_TRIGGER) - a user closing
        one Transaction would lose their save. See that rule's own header, line "including the
        known exposure on a deal with two Transactions, which is this rule's problem to surface,
        not this rule's problem to solve." This flow is where it is solved.

        KEYED ON Status__c = 'Closed', NOT Stage__c - same field and literal this flow's own
        trigger condition already used before this change, and the field
        Transaction_Stage_Closed_Sets_Status:21-25/35-39 and
        Has_Closed_Transaction__c:35-39 both name as the deliberate, explicit choice.
        Transaction_Stage_Closed_Sets_Status keeps Status__c synced from Stage__c for every
        writer (quick action, Path, API, data loader, seed script), so a plain Status__c = 'Closed'
        read here is trustworthy without also checking Stage__c.

        DOES NOT READ Opportunity.Has_Open_Transaction__c / Has_Closed_Transaction__c. Those
        flags are written by DealTransactionGateService from the Transaction__c trigger in the
        SAME transaction as this after-save flow, and after-trigger-vs-after-save-flow ordering
        is not something to assume without proof (platform Order of Execution steps 8 vs 13 make
        it LIKELY safe, per Transaction_Closed_Before_Closed_Won:71-78, but that note is about the
        VALIDATION RULE reading the flags after DealTransactionGateService has run, not about this
        flow). This element runs its own explicit Get Records against Transaction__c siblings
        instead of trusting a derived flag it did not itself order against.

        runInMode IS SystemModeWithoutSharing, EXPLICITLY, matching the identical shape already
        used by Wire_Verification_Rollup and NDA_Signed_Rollup for the same reason:
        Transaction__c is sharingModel Private (Transaction__c.object-meta.xml:165), and whoever
        saves one Transaction on a multi-Transaction deal is not necessarily the owner of, or
        shared into, its siblings. A user-mode Get Records here would silently under-count open
        siblings for a user who cannot see them, closing the deal early - the exact bug this
        change exists to remove, reintroduced through sharing instead of through logic. This also
        changes the enforcement mode of the pre-existing Close_Opportunity update (previously
        unspecified runInMode, which this repo has separately confirmed defaults to USER context)
        - accepted, because Opportunity.sharingModel is ReadWrite
        (Opportunity.object-meta.xml:165), so that write was never meaningfully sharing-gated, and
        Congratulate's Apex action (GroupNotifier) declares its own `without sharing` and is
        unaffected by flow runInMode either way.

        FOUR SCENARIOS THIS GUARD IS BUILT AGAINST:
          1. One Transaction, closes -> Get_Open_Sibling_Transactions finds nothing (no siblings
             at all) -> deal closes. Unchanged from pre-2026-09-02 behaviour.
          2. Two Transactions, first closes -> the second is still open and is not itself (Id
             NotEqualTo $Record.Id) -> deal does NOT close, and because Close_Opportunity is never
             reached, the Opportunity is never touched and Transaction_Closed_Before_Closed_Won
             never evaluates - the Transaction save succeeds cleanly. THIS ROW IS THE WHOLE POINT.
          3. Two Transactions, second closes -> the first is already Status__c = 'Closed' and is
             excluded by the NotEqualTo 'Closed' filter, not by the Id exclusion -> no open
             siblings found -> deal closes.
          4. Transaction closes, deal already Closed Won -> Close_Opportunity re-assigns the same
             StageName value; ISCHANGED(StageName) in Transaction_Closed_Before_Closed_Won (and in
             every sibling Closed-Won-adjacent rule) is false, so no rule evaluates and no error
             surfaces - a true no-op, unrelated to this guard.
    -->
    <actionCalls>
        <name>Congratulate</name>
        <label>Congratulate</label>
        <locationX>176</locationX>
        <locationY>408</locationY>
        <actionName>GroupNotifier</actionName>
        <actionType>apex</actionType>
        <flowTransactionModel>CurrentTransaction</flowTransactionModel>
        <inputParameters>
            <name>recipientGroup</name>
            <value>
                <stringValue>Acquisitions_Team</stringValue>
            </value>
        </inputParameters>
        <inputParameters>
            <name>title</name>
            <value>
                <stringValue>Deal closed - congratulations! 🎉</stringValue>
            </value>
        </inputParameters>
        <inputParameters>
            <name>body</name>
            <value>
                <stringValue>The transaction is complete. The deal moves to Bought/Closed.</stringValue>
            </value>
        </inputParameters>
        <inputParameters>
            <name>targetRecordId</name>
            <value>
                <elementReference>$Record.Opportunity__c</elementReference>
            </value>
        </inputParameters>
        <nameSegment>GroupNotifier</nameSegment>
    </actionCalls>
    <apiVersion>67.0</apiVersion>
    <decisions>
        <name>No_Open_Sibling_Transactions</name>
        <label>Any sibling Transaction still open?</label>
        <locationX>176</locationX>
        <locationY>210</locationY>
        <description>Added 2026-09-02 with the sibling guard. Only the No_Open_Siblings outcome reaches Close_Opportunity; the default (an open sibling was found) ends the flow without touching the Opportunity at all, so Transaction_Closed_Before_Closed_Won never evaluates on this save.</description>
        <defaultConnectorLabel>Open sibling exists - do not close yet</defaultConnectorLabel>
        <rules>
            <name>No_Open_Siblings</name>
            <conditionLogic>and</conditionLogic>
            <conditions>
                <leftValueReference>Get_Open_Sibling_Transactions.Id</leftValueReference>
                <operator>IsNull</operator>
                <rightValue>
                    <booleanValue>true</booleanValue>
                </rightValue>
            </conditions>
            <connector>
                <targetReference>Close_Opportunity</targetReference>
            </connector>
            <label>No open siblings</label>
        </rules>
    </decisions>
    <description>Closes the parent Opportunity when a Transaction__c on it reaches Status__c = 'Closed' - but ONLY when no OTHER Transaction on the same Opportunity is still open (Get_Open_Sibling_Transactions / No_Open_Sibling_Transactions, added 2026-09-02). Verified scenarios: (1) one Transaction closes -&gt; deal closes; (2) two Transactions, first closes -&gt; deal stays open, Transaction save succeeds cleanly; (3) two Transactions, second closes -&gt; deal closes; (4) Transaction closes while deal is already Closed Won -&gt; harmless no-op (ISCHANGED(StageName) is false). See the XML comment in this file for the full rationale.</description>
    <environments>Default</environments>
    <interviewLabel>Transaction Complete Close {!$Flow.CurrentDateTime}</interviewLabel>
    <label>Transaction Complete Close</label>
    <processType>AutoLaunchedFlow</processType>
    <recordLookups>
        <name>Get_Open_Sibling_Transactions</name>
        <label>Get Open Sibling Transactions</label>
        <locationX>176</locationX>
        <locationY>132</locationY>
        <assignNullValuesIfNoRecordsFound>true</assignNullValuesIfNoRecordsFound>
        <connector>
            <targetReference>No_Open_Sibling_Transactions</targetReference>
        </connector>
        <description>Finds any OTHER Transaction__c on the same Opportunity that has not reached Status__c = 'Closed'. Excludes the current record (Id NotEqualTo $Record.Id) so the Transaction being closed can never count itself as its own open sibling. getFirstRecordOnly is sufficient - this is an existence check, not a count.</description>
        <filterLogic>and</filterLogic>
        <filters>
            <field>Opportunity__c</field>
            <operator>EqualTo</operator>
            <value>
                <elementReference>$Record.Opportunity__c</elementReference>
            </value>
        </filters>
        <filters>
            <field>Id</field>
            <operator>NotEqualTo</operator>
            <value>
                <elementReference>$Record.Id</elementReference>
            </value>
        </filters>
        <filters>
            <field>Status__c</field>
            <operator>NotEqualTo</operator>
            <value>
                <stringValue>Closed</stringValue>
            </value>
        </filters>
        <getFirstRecordOnly>true</getFirstRecordOnly>
        <object>Transaction__c</object>
        <storeOutputAutomatically>true</storeOutputAutomatically>
    </recordLookups>
    <recordUpdates>
        <name>Close_Opportunity</name>
        <label>Close Opportunity</label>
        <locationX>176</locationX>
        <locationY>288</locationY>
        <connector>
            <targetReference>Congratulate</targetReference>
        </connector>
        <inputAssignments>
            <field>Deal_Category__c</field>
            <value>
                <stringValue>Closed</stringValue>
            </value>
        </inputAssignments>
        <inputAssignments>
            <field>Deal_Status__c</field>
            <value>
                <stringValue>Asset Under Management</stringValue>
            </value>
        </inputAssignments>
        <inputAssignments>
            <field>StageName</field>
            <value>
                <stringValue>Closed Won</stringValue>
            </value>
        </inputAssignments>
        <inputReference>$Record.Opportunity__r</inputReference>
    </recordUpdates>
    <runInMode>SystemModeWithoutSharing</runInMode>
    <start>
        <locationX>50</locationX>
        <locationY>0</locationY>
        <connector>
            <targetReference>Get_Open_Sibling_Transactions</targetReference>
        </connector>
        <doesRequireRecordChangedToMeetCriteria>true</doesRequireRecordChangedToMeetCriteria>
        <filterLogic>and</filterLogic>
        <filters>
            <field>Status__c</field>
            <operator>EqualTo</operator>
            <value>
                <stringValue>Closed</stringValue>
            </value>
        </filters>
        <filters>
            <field>Opportunity__c</field>
            <operator>IsNull</operator>
            <value>
                <booleanValue>false</booleanValue>
            </value>
        </filters>
        <object>Transaction__c</object>
        <recordTriggerType>CreateAndUpdate</recordTriggerType>
        <triggerType>RecordAfterSave</triggerType>
    </start>
    <status>Active</status>
</Flow>
